3347344a2ac9","event_uuid":"9e50dd3d-d0d0-4dc5-98de-accfc18839e8","position":{"commit_sha":"925d6da7aaeab37c0f72d1c721471298a5fa2729","position":"1795113515105871490-9e50dd3d-d0d0-4dc5-98de-accfc18839e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"224cb46145b393698ab87d98fb22fb4058bcccc9cb8c5f29af58d2adb14c6757","event_uuid":"4ee3e88e-b108-40e3-b4ed-ca7c180f9118","position":{"commit_sha":"ae3ada9098c9a2ce79fa183e8a98cf30c0b40335","position":"1795114389545128121-4ee3e88e-b108-40e3-b4ed-ca7c180f9118"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d83be73d304e0935da58f56075282d26d9862d84ac257520b97c2d3933e795a8","event_uuid":"58e70359-3ff8-42f2-8cf4-12fe3e861143","position":{"commit_sha":"ce257ddad6a20f586209edce47ea981c5453789e","position":"1795116819818302041-58e70359-3ff8-42f2-8cf4-12fe3e861143"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"095032dc53c1d5681cfec938d6bacafb68bdefd285d17309e581d4a4ed510964","event_uuid":"43633a79-20a0-4bfc-b44f-ec97bc251fc3","position":{"commit_sha":"ce257ddad6a20f586209edce47ea981c5453789e","position":"1795116819833270362-43633a79-20a0-4bfc-b44f-ec97bc251fc3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795112499766109190,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEpic nonblack-brigandish-guillemot replaces the repo-pinned op-cert trust file `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` with an optional per-environment trust list in each environment's own config (ADR 0125, sibling ADR task). Rebar's MCP server must never run without its list; today it trusts via `_opcert_trust_root` in `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`. So the list and its deployment land BEFORE the sibling story that stops reading the repo file. Sequencing: after the ADR task merges; the validity-only story builds on this merged commit.\n\n## Approach\n1. Config key `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` (tuple of strings, default empty = unset): field on `VerifyConfig` in `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` beside `require_environment` (line 164); coercer in `_SECTIONS[\"verify\"]` of `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` with marker `# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.trusted_opcert_keys — 0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90 (ADR 0125 per-environment trust list)`, placed like the `verify.plan_review_engine` marker; `(\"verify\", \"trusted_opcert_keys\")` joins `_EMPTY_ENV_FAULT_KEYS` so an empty `${VAR}` raises. New coercer `_as_trusted_key_list` in `src/rebar/_config_coercion.py` reuses `_as_str_tuple` (TOML array or comma-separated `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS`) and requires `<env_id> <key-type> <base64> [comment]` with decodable base64, else `ConfigError` naming the entry position.\n2. `verify_opcert_record` (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py` line 163), list set: trust root is the SSHSIG's embedded key (`rebar.attest.sshsig.embedded_public_key`). Order: undecodable envelope `invalid`; bad signature `mismatch`; wrong signed subject `mismatch` (`_opcert_subject_binding_error`); valid and bound but (principal, key type + body, comment ignored) not listed: new verdict `untrusted` (verified false, reason names key fingerprint and environment); listed: passes, trust basis `trust_list`. `verify.require_environment` applies first as today (`foreign_key`). If the list cannot be read or coerced, the helper fails closed (`untrusted`, reason names the config error), never \"unset\". List unset: unchanged in this story. Every op-cert result gains `signing_key` (null when no key can be extracted), the `SHA256:` fingerprint computed as `signer_key_id` in `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_authorship.py`. The check lives in a helper so `verify_opcert_record` stays under its complexity ceiling.\n3. Vocabulary: `untrusted` joins the verdict enums of `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json` (described, in the unverified group) and `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json`; `trust_list` joins `trust_basis`; `signing_key` is a described property. Regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` with `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`. Update the `verify_signature` ToolSpec in `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py`, the `plan_review_status` verdict lists in `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py`, the `_lib_identity.verify_signature` docstring (`src/rebar/_lib_identity.py`), `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json`, the verdict table and trust-basis prose in `docs/reuse-surface.md`, the exact verdict set in `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py`, and `_SIGNATURE_FAILURE_VERDICTS` in `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py`. `signature_findings` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py` reports `untrusted` as a MINOR finding beside `foreign_key`, naming key and environment.\n4. `opcert_signing_status` in `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`: list set means `expected` true, `matched` = (bound principal, signer key body) listed, and a new `trust_source: \"trust_list\"` field; list unset keeps the pin-file comparison (`trust_source: \"pin_file\"`).\n5. Deployment: `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS` in the `mcp` environment of `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` and as `-e` in `mcp_run_new` of `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (line 393), identical values listing the 3 keys now pinned: env `9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65` with `nava-opcert-prod` and `nava-opcert-prod rotated-20260907`, env `ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5` with `rebar-opcert`. Both files are in autodeploy's `MCP_PATHS`, so the merge rolls the container with no manual step.\n6. Document the key in `docs/config.md`; regenerate `docs/config-reference.md` (`scripts/gen_config_reference.py`), `docs/env-vars.md` (`scripts/gen_env_registry.py`) and `tests/golden/config_surface.json` (`scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py`).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`, `src/rebar/_config_coercion.py`, `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`\n- `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json`, `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json`, `src/rebar/types.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_identity.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py`\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`\n- `docs/config.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, `tests/golden/config_surface.json`, `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json`\n- tests: `tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py` (new), `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`, `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`, `tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py`\nOut of scope: pin-file readers, the file, `rebar trusted-env` (sibling stories); signing.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py`, real ed25519 keys from `ssh-keygen`. List set: listed pair `certified`, `trust_list`, correct `signing_key`; unlisted key `untrusted`; listed key under another principal `untrusted`; tampered payload or cross-ticket replay `mismatch`; `require_environment` naming another environment `foreign_key`; malformed list never `certified`. List unset: pinned-key certificate verifies as before. Config: malformed entry and empty env value raise `ConfigError`; a 3-entry comma-separated value parses to 3. Health: listed signer not degraded with `trust_source` `trust_list`; unlisted signer degraded. Validate: `untrusted` yields a MINOR `[SIGNATURE]` finding. Deploy: compose and `mcp_run_new` carry the same value, parsing to exactly the 3 pinned (env_id, key body) pairs; blue-green parity covers the new `-e`.\nPortability: pure-Python parsing and hashing; existing `ssh-keygen` verify path unchanged; no new subprocess, fd, path or permission handling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` set, a certificate by a listed key for its environment verifies with trust basis `trust_list`, and a valid certificate by an unlisted key gets `untrusted` (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py -q`).\n- [ ] With the list unset, existing op-cert verification is unchanged (checked: existing op-cert test modules pass under `make verify`).\n- [ ] The key is documented in `docs/config.md` and `docs/config-reference.md`, carries a `mechanism-ok` marker naming epic 0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] Compose `mcp` and autodeploy's `mcp_run_new` set `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS` to the same 3-key value (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py -q`).\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After autodeploy rolls this change, the live MCP `/health` `opcert` field reads `expected: true`, `matched: true`, `trust_source: \"trust_list\"` and no `error`.\n  provenance: environment=rebar Gerrit box i-00880b2c7f13527c5; principal=operator AWS profile frontier; privilege_posture=read-only SSM command running curl against the MCP loopback /health; instrument=aws ssm send-command + get-command-invocation — the health route is loopback-only, so no repository check can observe the deployed container.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"VerifyConfig.trusted_opcert_keys field"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"coercer, mechanism-ok marker, empty-env fault key"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_coercion.py","reason":"_as_trusted_key_list"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py","reason":"trust-list check, untrusted verdict, signing_key"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py","reason":"health against the trust list, trust_source"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json","reason":"untrusted, trust_list, signing_key"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":"untrusted verdict"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"regenerated from schemas"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py","reason":"verify_signature description"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"plan_review_status docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"plan_review_status docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_identity.py","reason":"verify_signature docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","reason":"untrusted signature finding"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"mcp REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"mcp_run_new -e REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document key"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"verdict table and trust basis prose"},{"path":"tests/golden/config_surface.json","reason":"regenerated config surface golden"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json","reason":"embedded copies"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py","reason":"deployment list"},{"path":"tests/